  Slot32's STREAM can move: its stride is the widest record of a group of 32,
  and the concatenation regroups at segment boundaries. Planes14's cannot — 14
  bytes per block, no bases table. What BOTH pay is `gs_off`, one u32 a fused
  row naming that row's centroid pair: 3.7 MB over the 72 groups, and it is the
  only byte fusion adds. It was missing from this ledger until 2026-09-10, which
  printed +0.00% and called that a verification (tests/planes_segment_matches_unfused.rs).
  Any gain BEYOND this would be a confounder, not a bonus.

